Cleanup order matters: delete the ASG first, confirm its instance is terminated, then delete the Launch Template.

## 8. Key Learnings

- A Launch Template defines how new EC2 instances are launched, but does not launch them itself.
- An Auto Scaling Group manages EC2 instance capacity and replaces unhealthy instances.
- Scaling policies determine when and how capacity changes. Without one, the ASG does not scale on load.
- Launch Templates, Auto Scaling Groups, and scaling policies work together to manage EC2 capacity.
- Deleting an ASG terminates its instances and removes its scaling alarms.
- Cleanup is an essential part of working with AWS to avoid unexpected charges.

